{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788404201,"nonce":"73LJj71D0nIETtK2eeJq08b5TlA=","title":"install verb: a MinifiedThing cannot be placed, so G5 is unreachable","message":"## What happened\n\nRun openrun-20260902, Spring 1 of 5501. `things {def:\"MinifiedThing\"}` reports\n**count 1** — a wooden small sculpture (id 12500, normal quality) sitting at\n(108,105) inside the base.\n\nThe open-ended run contract grades G5 as *\"`MinifiedThing` count is **0**, and no\ncolonist carries `Unsightly environment`\"*. There is no verb that can move that\ncount to zero:\n\n- `build {thing:12500, at:[104,104]}` — refused, `missing required arg 'def'`.\n  `build` has no `thing` form at all.\n- `build {def:\"SculptureSmall\", …}` — refused, and correctly:\n  `'SculptureSmall' is not BuildableByPlayer (its designationCategory is null,\n  so no Designator_Build exists for it and it has no blueprintDef either)`.\n  A sculpture is *installed*, never *built*.\n- Nothing in `rwa verbs` covers it. `grep -n 'install\\|Minified' BuildVerbs.cs\n  PlaceVerbs.cs Siting.cs` finds only two comments in `Siting.cs`\n  (lines 25, 215–216) that already reference\n  `RimWorld/Designator_Install.CanDesignateCell` — the gate is known to the\n  code, it just has no verb in front of it.\n\nSo a finished sculpture is stuck as an item forever, which is exactly the\nfailure G5 was written against: run m1 left five sculptures in a crate for 66\ndays. An agent that reads the trip-wire, queries `MinifiedThing` daily as\ninstructed, and *sees the non-zero count* still has no move to make.\n\n## Why it is more than G5\n\n`MinifiedThing` is the carrier for every minifiable building, not just art —\nbeds, tables, benches, braziers. Any of them acquired from a trader, a quest\nreward, or an uninstall is unplaceable by the agent today. The colony can\nreceive furniture it can never set down.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A verb places a minified thing: either `build {thing:\u003cid\u003e, at:[x,z], rot?}`\n  gains a `thing` form, or a dedicated `install {thing, at, rot?}` ships.\n- The gate is RimWorld's own and is cited: `Designator_Install.CanDesignateCell`\n  plus `GenConstruct.CanPlaceBlueprintAt`, in the same shape `build` already\n  uses — a refusal names the blocking clause rather than inventing one.\n- It creates a **`Blueprint_Install`**, not a new thing: the minified item is\n  consumed by the install job, and the placed building keeps the item's own\n  quality, hit points and stuff. A verb that spawns a fresh sculpture instead\n  would silently launder quality and is not acceptable.\n- Reinstalling an already-placed minifiable building (the uninstall→install\n  round trip) is out of scope here unless it falls out for free; say which in\n  the result.\n- `things {def:\"MinifiedThing\"}` reads 0 after the install job completes, on a\n  live bench, with the sculpture standing where it was asked for.\n- Refused cleanly when the target cell cannot take it, with `error.class`\n  `refused` and the cell's blocker named — the same envelope `build` returns.","files":null}]}